  clock: 2  # 087a
  nonce: 087a  # 087a
  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). CURRENT, EFFECT RE-STATED. getenv -> mylib.ship with a provenance: community --taint-sinks file declaring mylib.ship trust_level: trusted: the trust is honoured (trusted_sink_flows=1) and the details credit 'a sink the project's catalogue declares trusted' (verify_claims.py:6229) while the file is listed under tiers.community and user_supplied is false. A community trusted builtins.eval row is dropped (the community taint layer only adds, taint.py:2593-2603). 'Trusted' and YAML true are inert -- deliberate per WI-lukoz (spec ~:1049); a typo fails strict. OWNER RULING 2026-10-25: withhold trust_level: trusted from community files and name the withheld rows, as community sanitizers are. Ground: ADR-0061 ruling 2 ('the test is what a row can do'); trusted can only take flows out of evidence_count (verify_claims.py:6131-6132), so it is purely the removing half, in the sanitizer column; the spec counts only --taint-sinks / extra_catalogs: as project sink catalogues. The comparison is the same row with vs without its removing effect, as ruling 2's crypto-sanitizer consequence uses -- not file vs no file. Cost today zero: no shipped sink file is community or declares trusted; the case arises when a user copies a community file, which ruling 3 keeps community. Fix: a community flag on TaintSink; withhold and name (mirror withheld_sanitizers); fix the misattributed 'project's catalogue' clause. trust_level validation stays optional polish. Minor: spec ~:1049 omits the taint_sinks.d/ yours channel (honoured correctly; spec update only). Refs: taint.py:1825 (no validation), :319 (TRUST_LEVEL_TRUSTED). P3 kept."  # 087a
